<span data-as=3D"p">A <a href=3D"https://langchain-ai.github.io/langgraph/r=
eference/graphs.md#langgraph.graph.StateGraph" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"nor=
eferrer" class=3D"link">StateGraph</a> accepts a <a href=3D"https://referen=
ce.langchain.com/python/langchain/middleware/#langchain.agents.middleware.A=
gentMiddleware.state_schema" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noreferrer" class=3D"=
link"><code>state_schema</code></a> argument on initialization that specifi=
es the =E2=80=9Cshape=E2=80=9D of the state that the nodes in the graph can=
 access and update.</span>
<span data-as=3D"p">In our examples, we typically use a python-native <code=
>TypedDict</code> or <a href=3D"https://docs.python.org/3/library/dataclass=
es.html" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noreferrer" class=3D"link"><code>dataclas=
s</code></a> for <code>state_schema</code>, but <a href=3D"https://referenc=
e.langchain.com/python/langchain/middleware/#langchain.agents.middleware.Ag=
entMiddleware.state_schema" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noreferrer" class=3D"l=
ink"><code>state_schema</code></a> can be any <a href=3D"https://docs.pytho=
n.org/3/library/stdtypes.html#type-objects" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"norefe=
rrer" class=3D"link">type</a>.</span>
<span data-as=3D"p">Here, we=E2=80=99ll see how a <a href=3D"https://docs.p=
ydantic.dev/latest/api/base_model/" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noreferrer" cl=
ass=3D"link">Pydantic BaseModel</a> can be used for <a href=3D"https://refe=
rence.langchain.com/python/langchain/middleware/#langchain.agents.middlewar=
e.AgentMiddleware.state_schema" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noreferrer" class=
=3D"link"><code>state_schema</code></a> to add run-time validation on <stro=
ng>inputs</strong>.</span>
