<span data-as=3D"p">When creating a graph with a loop, we require a mechani=
sm for terminating execution. This is most commonly done by adding a <a cla=
ss=3D"link" href=3D"https://docs.langchain.com/oss/python/langgraph/graph-a=
pi#conditional-edges">conditional edge</a> that routes to the <a class=3D"l=
ink" href=3D"https://docs.langchain.com/oss/python/langgraph/graph-api#end-=
node">END</a> node once we reach some termination condition.</span>
<span data-as=3D"p">You can also set the graph recursion limit when invokin=
g or streaming the graph. The recursion limit sets the number of <a class=
=3D"link" href=3D"https://docs.langchain.com/oss/python/langgraph/graph-api=
#graphs">supersteps</a> that the graph is allowed to execute before it rais=
es an error. Read more about the concept of recursion limits <a class=3D"li=
nk" href=3D"https://docs.langchain.com/oss/python/langgraph/graph-api#recur=
sion-limit">here</a>.</span>
